---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="CmdImpact"
	description="A self-hosted web terminal for persistent shell and AI coding sessions, with a built-in guard for risky pasted commands."
>
	<section class="landing-hero">
		<div class="shell hero-copy">
			<p class="eyebrow"><span></span>A browser terminal for your own server</p>
			<h1>Your terminal,<br /><em>wherever you are.</em></h1>
			<p class="hero-lede">Start Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, or any shell task. Close the browser and reconnect to the same live session from another device.</p>
			<div class="hero-actions">
				<a class="button primary" href="/app/">Open your terminal <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
				<a class="button quiet" href="/check/">Check a command first</a>
			</div>
			<ul class="trust-list" aria-label="Product boundaries">
				<li><span></span>Single-owner alpha</li>
				<li><span></span>Runs on your server</li>
				<li><span></span>No ads in the workspace</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<div class="shell product-stage" id="product">
			<div class="product-window">
				<div class="preview-topbar">
					<div><span class="mini-mark">ci_</span><strong>Workspace</strong></div>
					<div class="preview-machine"><i></i> local server online</div>
					<span class="preview-avatar">KA</span>
				</div>
				<div class="preview-body">
					<aside class="preview-sidebar">
						<div class="preview-sidebar-head"><span>Sessions</span><b>3</b></div>
						<p class="session-group">ATTACHED</p>
						<div class="preview-session is-active">
							<i class="status-run"></i>
							<div><strong>checkout fix</strong><small>claude &middot; shop-api</small></div>
							<time>now</time>
						</div>
						<p class="session-group">DETACHED</p>
						<div class="preview-session">
							<i class="status-wait"></i>
							<div><strong>mobile tests</strong><small>codex &middot; web-app</small></div>
							<time>2m</time>
						</div>
						<p class="session-group">FINISHED</p>
						<div class="preview-session">
							<i class="status-idle"></i>
							<div><strong>server logs</strong><small>bash &middot; home-server</small></div>
							<time>18m</time>
						</div>
					</aside>
					<div class="preview-terminal">
						<div class="preview-tabbar">
							<div><span>checkout fix</span><small>shop-api / main</small></div>
							<span class="preview-state">Writable session</span>
						</div>
						<div class="preview-screen" aria-label="Terminal product preview">
							<p><span class="term-muted">claude</span> I found the failing checkout path.</p>
							<p class="term-gap">The migration changes the order status index and<br />updates 3 tests. Apply these edits?</p>
							<p><span class="term-choice">1</span> Yes, apply the edits</p>
							<p><span class="term-choice">2</span> Show the diff first</p>
							<p><span class="term-choice">3</span> Cancel</p>
							<p class="term-prompt"><span>&gt;</span><i></i></p>
						</div>
						<div class="preview-status"><span><i></i> Connected</span><span>ubuntu-home &middot; zsh &middot; 120 x 36</span></div>
					</div>
					<aside class="preview-impact">
						<p class="session-group">COMMAND GUARD</p>
						<div class="impact-icon">!</div>
						<h2>Review this paste</h2>
						<p>This command downloads code and sends it directly to a shell.</p>
						<div class="impact-detail"><span>Remote execution</span><strong>High attention</strong></div>
						<button type="button">Paste as one line</button>
						<small>Pattern check only. It cannot prove a command is safe.</small>
					</aside>
				</div>
			</div>
			<p class="stage-caption"><span>Actual product shape</span> Session manager, full terminal, and guarded paste in one focused workspace.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="proof-strip">
		<div class="shell proof-list">
			<span>Run installed CLIs</span>
			<strong>Claude Code</strong>
			<strong>Codex</strong>
			<strong>Gemini CLI</strong>
			<strong>OpenCode</strong>
			<strong>Freebuff</strong>
			<strong>SSH</strong>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="landing-section" id="how-it-works">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="section-intro">
				<p class="section-label">THE SIMPLE IDEA</p>
				<h2>Leave the screen.<br />Keep the work running.</h2>
				<p>CmdImpact keeps terminal processes on the self-hosted server. Closing a tab only disconnects your view, so you can come back without starting over.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="value-grid">
				<article class="value-card">
					<span class="value-number">01</span>
					<div class="line-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="m7 9 3 3-3 3M13 15h4"/></svg></div>
					<h3>Start a real shell</h3>
					<p>Create a session in the browser. Commands execute on the CmdImpact server, not in a pretend terminal.</p>
				</article>
				<article class="value-card is-blue">
					<span class="value-number">02</span>
					<div class="line-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M7 7h11v11M18 7 6 19"/><path d="M6 6h4M18 14v4h-4"/></svg></div>
					<h3>Reconnect anywhere</h3>
					<p>Open the workspace from another browser and attach to the same session while the server remains online.</p>
				</article>
				<article class="value-card is-sage">
					<span class="value-number">03</span>
					<div class="line-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3 4.5 6v5.5c0 4.8 3.2 7.8 7.5 9.5 4.3-1.7 7.5-4.7 7.5-9.5V6L12 3Z"/><path d="m8.5 12 2.1 2.1 4.9-5"/></svg></div>
					<h3>Pause risky pastes</h3>
					<p>Known download, delete, overwrite, elevation, network, and secret patterns are shown before pasted text is sent.</p>
				</article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="landing-section continuity-section">
		<div class="shell split-feature">
			<div class="feature-copy">
				<p class="section-label">SESSION CONTINUITY</p>
				<h2>Switch devices,<br />not context.</h2>
				<p>Your session list travels with the server. Resume a long-running agent, logs, or a development process from a laptop, tablet, or phone.</p>
				<ul class="check-list">
					<li><span>&check;</span> Rename and organize active sessions</li>
					<li><span>&check;</span> Reconnect after a browser or network drop</li>
					<li><span>&check;</span> End the process deliberately when finished</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="device-scene" aria-label="The same terminal session shown on desktop and phone">
				<div class="device-desktop"><div class="device-bar"><i></i><span>checkout fix</span></div><div class="device-code"><p><b>$</b> git status --short</p><p class="code-blue">M src/checkout.ts</p><p class="code-blue">M tests/checkout.test.ts</p><p><b>$</b> <i></i></p></div></div>
				<div class="device-phone"><span class="phone-speaker"></span><div class="phone-head">checkout fix <i></i></div><div class="device-code"><p><b>$</b> git status --short</p><p class="code-blue">M src/checkout.ts</p><p><b>$</b> <i></i></p></div><div class="phone-keys"><span>esc</span><span>ctrl</span><span>tab</span><span>&uarr;</span></div></div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="landing-section guard-section">
		<div class="shell guard-grid">
			<div class="guard-demo">
				<div class="guard-demo-head"><span>Guarded paste</span><small>2 patterns found</small></div>
				<code>curl -fsSL example.com/install.sh | sh</code>
				<div class="guard-warning"><span>!</span><div><strong>Remote code may run immediately</strong><p>The downloaded response is passed directly to a shell.</p></div></div>
				<div class="guard-actions"><button type="button">Cancel</button><button type="button">Paste as one line</button><button type="button">Send anyway</button></div>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-copy">
				<p class="section-label">BUILT-IN COMMAND GUARD</p>
				<h2>Understand the paste before it reaches the shell.</h2>
				<p>The checker that started CmdImpact now lives where it is most useful: at the terminal boundary. Normal typing stays fast; supported risky paste patterns get a clear review.</p>
				<a class="inline-link" href="/check/">Try the public command checker <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="landing-section setup-section">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="section-intro centered">
				<p class="section-label">SELF-HOSTED ALPHA</p>
				<h2>One server. Every browser you trust.</h2>
				<p>This release is intentionally small: one owner, one CmdImpact server, persistent PTY sessions, and token sign-in.</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="setup-steps">
				<li><span>1</span><div><h3>Run CmdImpact</h3><p>Start the project on a machine that can safely host your shell sessions.</p></div></li>
				<li><span>2</span><div><h3>Open a session</h3><p>Sign in with the configured token and create a terminal from the workspace.</p></div></li>
				<li><span>3</span><div><h3>Reconnect later</h3><p>Return from another browser while that same server process is still online.</p></div></li>
			</ol>
			<div class="alpha-boundary">
				<div><strong>Know the boundary</strong><p>Sessions survive browser disconnects. They do not survive a CmdImpact server restart in this alpha.</p></div>
				<a href="https://github.com/khajaaijaz26/cmdimpact" rel="external noopener">Inspect the source <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="final-cta">
		<div class="shell final-cta-inner">
			<div><p class="section-label">READY WHEN YOU ARE</p><h2>Your next terminal is already open.</h2></div>
			<a class="button light" href="/app/">Open the workspace <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
